implementationPlan.description:
Write the regression test first. Create packages/moe-daemon/src/state/finalizingCloseRetry.test.ts with your own editor (Write on Claude, apply_patch on codex exec), never a shell copy or a subagent: the TOOL witness matters at landing (global rail). Start from the architect's dry-run prototype /mnt/d/moe-scratch/plan-efe07ce5/finalizingCloseRetry.test.ts (151 lines, 11 tests, ToolTestHarness).

The fixture seeds task-1 in REVIEW, unassigned, reopenCount 1, both plan steps COMPLETED and workStartedAt as the round start. worker-1 is registered IDLE. Its attempt on task-1 is opened with openAttempt (workspaceMode 'worktree' unless the case says otherwise), then set finalizing with setAttemptPhase, the same pattern as tools/finalizeAttempt.test.ts:424-429.

Cases:
(a) it.each over the three close paths. Each must leave the attempt [[1,'closed']] and the task WORKING, unassigned, reopenCount 1, implementationPlan and stepsCompleted unchanged. landingRetry must equal { reason: 'contention', paths: [], rescueRef: 'refs/heads/moe/task/task-1', targetTip: null, count: 1, at: any string }, plus one moe-daemon comment naming the attempt id, worker-1, 'no completion recorded', 'Landing unlanded (contention) 1 time(s)' and 'task WORKING'. The paths:
  - the moe.deregister_worker tool (deregisterWorkerTool handler, reason terminal_closed, result success and releasedTaskIds []);
  - the DEAD-record prune: updateWorker DEAD, then state.deleteWorker;
  - the startup purge: updateWorker DEAD, reconcileRunningAttempts, then state.purgeAllWorkers.
(b) A completion recorded before this round started does not count, so the row still routes.
(c) it.each, the plain close is kept (attempt closed; status, assignee, comment count unchanged; landingRetry undefined) for:
  - a completion recorded this round;
  - a 'shared' attempt;
  - a mode-less (legacy) attempt;
  - a row no longer in REVIEW (WORKING);
  - a REVIEW row another seat holds (assignedWorkerId 'qa-1').
(d) A prior landingRetry with count 2 becomes count 3, and the row goes BLOCKED with blockedFromStatus 'WORKING', exactly as finalize's unlanded route.
(e) updateTask rejected once (vi.spyOn mockRejectedValueOnce): deregister still succeeds, the attempt is closed, the row stays REVIEW and landingRetry stays undefined.

RED: run the step-5 checkRef now, before steps 2-3. It must exit 1 at its first stage with exactly 5 failures in this file ((a) x3, (b) and (d)) and 6 passes. The architect's run at d1062cb0 gave 'Tests 5 failed | 110 passed (115)' across the 3 focused files. Put your RED in the step summary.

Sync the docs and comments. Use your own editor (Edit on Claude, apply_patch on codex), never Serena for docs/ (it ignores the folder) and never a shell write. Re-grep each heading first; the line numbers are from d1062cb0. Edit only these spots; two open rows (87cba58c, 1f84f4e4) own other docs/MCP_SERVER.md sections.
(1) docs/MCP_SERVER.md `### moe.deregister_worker` (:2166). In the '**Closes its own finalizing attempts, first.**' list, add a bullet after '**It is not evidence of a landing.**', titled '**A worktree landing with nothing recorded goes back for a retry.**'. Its content:
  - the predicate: a worktree attempt (`workspaceMode: 'worktree'`) whose task is in REVIEW, held by no seat, with no `completion` entry in `task.commits` for the current work round (the round qa_approve's commit gate counts);
  - why: nothing is known to have published, and QA's landed gate would park the row BLOCKED;
  - the routing, exactly as finalize_attempt's `unlanded`: reason `contention`, no paths, `rescueRef` = the task branch `refs/heads/moe/task/<taskId>`, no target tip. landingRetry is set, one moe-daemon comment names the attempt, and the row goes WORKING, unassigned, keeping reopenCount and its completed steps (BLOCKED on the third unlanded landing in a row);
  - the next worker's pre-flight merges the target and prompts `LANDING-RETRY: contention`;
  - every other row keeps the plain close (a completion recorded for the round, a shared-mode or mode-less attempt, a row not in REVIEW, one another seat holds);
  - no git reads (the receipt replay settles an unrecorded publish); a failed routing write is logged and the close stands;
  - removing a DEAD record routes the same way.
(2) docs/MCP_SERVER.md `### moe.finalize_attempt` (:602), the '**Every end of a finalizing attempt.**' list. Item 2 (deregister_worker) gains that such a close also routes the row back for a landing retry, as `unlanded` does (see moe.deregister_worker). Item 5 (removing a DEAD record) gains 'with the same landing-retry routing as item 2'.
(3) docs/SCHEMA.md:
  - :501 landingRetry comment: set by finalize_attempt 'unlanded', or by the finalizing close of a worktree landing with no completion recorded.
  - :847: replace 'Only `moe.finalize_attempt` writes it: ...' with the two writers: finalize 'unlanded', and closing a worktree attempt whose REVIEW task has no completion recorded for its round (moe.deregister_worker, or removing a DEAD worker record), with reason 'contention' and the task branch as rescueRef. Landed and nothing-to-commit still null it.
  - :855 rescueRef comment: a refs/moe/rescue/<taskId>/... ref, or the task branch refs/heads/moe/task/<taskId> when a finalizing close set the retry.
(4) packages/moe-daemon/src/types/schema.ts, comment-only: the :1063 landingRetry doc comment ('finalize_attempt alone sets ...') names both writers, and the :873 rescueRef comment adds the task-branch case.
